android-kitkat-tls12

Own code (scripts, installer, the symbol and label helpers, the default-factory class, the SSLv3 filter module, the
build and test tools) is licensed under the Apache License 2.0; see LICENSE.

The patches modify third-party projects and keep their licences:

- external/openssl (OpenSSL 1.0.1u and the backported fixes from later OpenSSL releases): the OpenSSL License and
  the original SSLeay License (the dual licence of OpenSSL 1.x); the full text is the LICENSE file of OpenSSL 1.0.1u
  (openssl-1.0.1u.tar.gz from openssl.org) and the NOTICE in the openssl zip. The backported fixes come from later
  OpenSSL releases: 1.0.2 and 1.1.x are under the same OpenSSL/SSLeay licence, 3.x under the Apache License 2.0.
- libcore (core.jar, core-libart.jar, conscrypt.jar, libjavacrypto.so): the Apache License 2.0, with parts from
  Apache Harmony (Apache License 2.0) and Bouncy Castle (MIT-style licence); see libcore's NOTICE in AOSP.
- external/okhttp (okhttp.jar): the Apache License 2.0.

Layer D binaries are built from the published Maven artifact org.conscrypt:conscrypt-android:2.6-alpha2:

- Conscrypt (https://github.com/google/conscrypt): the Apache License 2.0, with parts from Netty and Apache Harmony.
- BoringSSL, linked statically into libkktls_conscrypt_jni.so (https://boringssl.googlesource.com/boringssl): its
  LICENSE at the commit Conscrypt 2.6-alpha2 was built from, including the OpenSSL/SSLeay licences of the code it
  inherited and the fiat-crypto licence. conscrypt/NOTICE holds the complete texts.

The CA store (cacerts/) is generated from the Mozilla root store (NSS certdata, as published by curl at
https://curl.se/ca/cacert.pem) and is licensed under the Mozilla Public License 2.0.

The static helpers kktls-symcheck and kktls-util in the recovery zips link the bionic C library of AOSP 4.4 (BSD-style
licences; see its NOTICE in AOSP).

Every recovery zip of a release carries a NOTICE file with the full licence texts for the files it installs; a
java-patched zip written by the jar patcher carries the donor java zip's NOTICE behind a note that its jars are the
device's own with the set's classes replaced. The jar patcher zip (kktls-jarpatch-<rel>.zip) is a host tool, not a
recovery zip: it carries this repository's LICENSE.

The jar patcher (tools/jarpatch/) runs smali and baksmali 2.5.2 (https://github.com/JesusFreke/smali, BSD-3-Clause;
the fat jars also bundle Guava and JCommander, Apache-2.0, ANTLR, BSD, and StringTemplate, BSD). They are not part of
this repository or the release zips: tools/jarpatch/fetch-smali.sh downloads them at run time from the upstream
author's downloads and checks their pinned sha256.

busybox (GPL-2.0) is not part of this repository or the release zips. tools/install-adb.sh downloads a static
upstream build from busybox.net at run time (source: https://busybox.net/downloads/busybox-1.31.0.tar.bz2), pushes
it to the device for the duration of the run and deletes it afterwards.
